---
description: Feature-branch PRs, signed commits, no push to main, no AI attribution
alwaysApply: true
---

# Shipping changes

- **Never push `main`.** Every change is a feature-branch PR. Fetch immediately, then
  `git checkout -b <name> origin/main` in one step. Confirm `git log --oneline -1` is the
  origin/main you expect.
- `git checkout -b X origin/main` sets upstream to **main**. Always push with an explicit
  refspec: `git push origin HEAD:refs/heads/<branch>`. Verify
  `git config --get branch.<branch>.merge` is `refs/heads/<branch>`.
- Rebase on `origin/main` before pushing. Don't merge stale. A PR is tested merged with main.
- Signed commits (SSH). Local `%G?` may show `N` — fine. Confirm the signature blob exists
  when signing is configured.
- Use the GitHub noreply committer
  (`140616733+Ndevu12@users.noreply.github.com`). A private Gmail committer is rejected
  (GH007).
- Name paths in `git add`. Never `git add -A` without reading `git status --porcelain`.
- Never write a session note, plan, or scratch file inside the repository.
- PR body: short. Defect, change, proof. Never how. Bare `Closes #NNNN` on its own line when
  the issue is on this repo.
- No AI / Cursor attribution anywhere. Before every `git commit` / `gh pr create|edit`,
  grep the message:
  `grep -ciE 'Co-Authored-By|Claude-Session|Generated with|claude\.ai/code|Made with Cursor|🤖'`
  Non-zero → rewrite before committing.
- Don't over-produce PRs. Align first, then ship a focused PR. Adjacent work goes in the
  open PR, not a parallel one off main.
- Merging is the maintainer's. Never `--admin`-merge.
- This repo has no CHANGELOG yet. Do not invent one in a conventions PR. When a user-visible
  product change ships, add `CHANGELOG.md` `[Unreleased]` in that same PR and describe what
  the user observes, not the implementation.
